$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"SSH"$$FG$

An SSH-2 client: interactive shells, one-off commands, Ed25519 public-key authentication, and the transport $LK,"Git",A="FI:::/Doc/Git.DD"$ uses for ssh urls.

$FG,4$No host-key checking.$FG$  The client accepts any server key, the same posture as the TLS stack.  That stops passive eavesdropping but not an active man-in-the-middle.  Typed passwords are echoed in the clear.

$FG,5$--- Load it ---$FG$

The network stack must be up first ($LK,"Net Start",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Start.ZC"$).  Then:

$ID,2$$FG,2$#include "C:/Home/Net/Programs/SSH/SSH"$FG$$ID,-2$

That pulls in the transport, SHA-512, Ed25519, auth, channels, keygen and the terminal.  Check the crypto before trusting key auth:

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSHCryptoTest;$FG$              SHA-512 + Ed25519 known-answer tests.  Both must be green.
$FG,2$SSHTransportTest("HOST", 22);$FG$   Handshake + cipher against a real server.$ID,-2$

SSHTransportTest prints one [ssh] line per stage.  If it stops early, the last line names the stage that failed.

$FG,5$--- Keys ---$FG$

Do this once, then stop typing passwords.

$FG,3$1. Generate$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSHKeyGen;$FG$$ID,-2$

Makes an Ed25519 keypair, saves it, loads it into the in-memory agent and prints the authorized_keys line.  Keys live in a $UL,1$visible$UL,0$ directory -- ZealOS has no hidden dotfolders:

$ID,2$C:/Home/Config/SSH/Ed25519.key    private: raw seed(32) + public(32)
C:/Home/Config/SSH/Ed25519.pub    the authorized_keys line$ID,-2$

$FG,3$2. Install it on the server$FG$

Copy the printed ssh-ed25519 line into the account's ~/.ssh/authorized_keys:

$ID,2$mkdir -p ~/.ssh && chmod 700 ~/.ssh
echo 'ssh-ed25519 AAAA... YKD@zealos' >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys$ID,-2$

To get the text out of a VM, start the clipboard bridge ($FG,2$ClipStart;$FG$ -- $LK,"Clip.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/Clip/Clip.ZC"$), run $FG,2$SSHKeyShow;$FG$, select the printed line and press Ctrl+C.

$FG,3$3. After a reboot$FG$

The key file persists; the agent does not.  Reload it:

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSHKeyLoad;$FG$$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- Shell ---$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSH;$FG$                              Prompts for host, user, password.
$FG,2$SSH("192.168.1.10");$FG$               Prompts for user, password.
$FG,2$SSH("192.168.1.10", 22, "root");$FG$   Key auth if a key is loaded, else prompts.$ID,-2$

$FG,4$Shift+Esc$FG$ quits the session.  The terminal is a scrolling DolDoc view, not a real pty: shells, ls, cat and git are fine, vim and htop look rough.

$FG,5$--- One command ---$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,2$SSHRun("192.168.1.10", 22, "root", "PASSWORD", "uname -a");$FG$$ID,-2$

Prints the output, then the exit status.  SSHRun uses password auth.

$FG,5$--- Command reference ---$FG$

$ID,2$SSH(host, port=22, user=NULL)     Interactive shell.  Shift+Esc quits.
SSHRun(host, port, user, pw, cmd) Run one command over password auth.
SSHTransportTest(host, port=22)   Handshake + cipher smoke test, inline stages.
SSHCryptoTest                     SHA-512 + Ed25519 self-test.
SSHKeyGen                         Generate, save and load a key; print the authorized_keys line.
SSHKeyLoad                        Load the saved key into the agent.
SSHKeyShow                        Print the public authorized_keys line.$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- Troubleshooting ---$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,4$Stops at ECDH$FG$ -- algorithm mismatch.  The client offers curve25519-sha256 and chacha20-poly1305 only; a server with both disabled is unreachable.

$FG,4$Authentication failed$FG$ -- wrong password, the key is not in the server's authorized_keys, or the account is disallowed (root login off).

$FG,4$Long freeze$FG$ -- the handshake blocks the terminal.  From a QEMU guest, a LAN host is reachable only if the host machine can reach it.

$FG,4$SSHCryptoTest red$FG$ -- do not use key auth; the crypto build is wrong.$ID,-2$

$FG,5$--- Supported / not ---$FG$

$FG,2$Supported:$FG$ SSH-2 transport (curve25519-sha256, chacha20-poly1305), password auth, Ed25519 public-key auth, session channels, pty + shell, exec, an in-memory key agent.

$FG,2$Not yet:$FG$ host-key verification, key passphrases, RSA/ECDSA keys, agent forwarding, port forwarding, a full ANSI terminal.

$FG,5$--- Source ---$FG$

$ID,2$$LK,"SSH.ZC",A="FI:::/Home/Net/Programs/SSH/SSH.ZC"$           loader
